# Build context for docker/Dockerfile. The context is the repository root
# (docker-compose.yml sets `context: ..`), so without this file Docker would
# ship ~2 GB to the daemon — .venv alone is 1.7 GB and data/ is 219 MB.
#
# Posture: exclude everything the running API does not need. What survives is
# src/, pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md and LICENSE.

# --- Environments and caches (rebuilt inside the image) ---
.venv
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Version control and tooling metadata ---
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.python-version

# --- Data and ML artifacts: NEVER inside the image ---
# The dataset is DVC-managed and the API never reads it. The local registry is
# excluded on purpose: the model is pulled at runtime from the MLflow service,
# so baking mlruns/ or mlflow.db in would tie this image to one model version
# and force a rebuild on every promotion.
data/
mlruns/
mlflow.db
models/
reports/
logs/
.dvc/
.dvcignore
dvc.yaml
dvc.lock

# --- Training-time config ---
# Read only by load_threshold() on the registration path; the serving threshold
# travels inside the packaged artifact. Verified: `import src.api.main`
# succeeds with params.yaml absent.
params.yaml

# --- Development and documentation ---
notebooks/
tests/
docs/
project_context/
pipelines/
Makefile
main.py

# --- Agent-local files (already git-ignored) ---
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# --- Local env overrides; only .env.example is tracked ---
docker/.env
